# Source documents go in this folder. The folder is tracked; its contents are not.
#
# They are client material and stay out of git deliberately. The list below is
# the record of what belongs here, so an empty folder is not a mystery.
#
# WHERE THEY COME FROM
#
#   Google Drive, "REB Document (Dalhousie University)", inside the project
#   handover folder. Owned by shakara.innovates@gmail.com.
#   https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1YvlM62Ije015ZFtFE3AmDCR9VUtMP7l_
#
#   Download the whole folder from Drive and unzip it here. Keep the filenames
#   exactly as they are: lib/kb/config.ts classifies documents by filename, and
#   a renamed file is classified as 'other' and cited by its bare filename.
#
# WHAT IS IN IT (15 files, verified 2026-08-06)
#
#   The form, and the spine of the build
#     application-human-ethics-prospective-research.docx
#
#   Guidance
#     reb-application-guidelines-for-prospective-research.pdf
#     hints-for-research-recruitment-messages.pdf            (+ -2 duplicate)
#
#   Templates
#     consent-form-template-online-survey.pdf
#     consent-form-prospective-research-data-collection.pdf
#     consent-form-secondary-personal-records.pdf            (+ -2 duplicate)
#     consent-form-secondary-research-existing-records.pdf   (+ -2 duplicate)
#     consent-form-data-sharing-repository-future-research.pdf
#     confidentiality-agreement-template.pdf                 (+ -2 duplicate)
#
#   Test material, not guidance. Never cite these to a researcher.
#     Draft Research Proposal_ Community Retrofit Readiness and Derisking Framework.docx
#     Future Civics - Braindump - REB CHAT.docx
#
# Four files arrive as -2 duplicates of a file already listed. Drop them in as
# they are. De-duplication is on content hash, not filename, so they cost
# nothing and removing them by hand risks removing the wrong copy.
#
# NOT HERE, AND NOT NEEDED HERE
#
#   TCPS 2. It is not in the Drive folder and does not need to be. It is a
#   public document published chapter by chapter at ethics.gc.ca, and the
#   knowledge base routes by form section to a named chapter rather than
#   searching for similar passages, so the chapters are read from source at the
#   point the mapping is built. See docs/decisions.md.
